#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-02.png", width: 344pt), 144.5pt, 88pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(560.16pt, 30.96pt, "2 ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 59.76pt, "and programmable counters used in our experiments of digital ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 71.28pt, "qubit control [17].")
  #line-at(139.68pt, 71.28pt, "These chips were fabricated using ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 82.68pt, "SEEQC’s SFQuClass fabrication process with a critical ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 94.92pt, "current density of 10 ")
  #line-at(157.68pt, 94.92pt, "A/")
  #line-at(173.28pt, 94.92pt, "m")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(181.08pt, 91.44pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(184.32pt, 94.92pt, ". This is optimized for ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 106.44pt, "integration with qubit chips operating in a 20 mK cryogenic ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 117.96pt, "environment [23], side-by-side with SEEQC’s qubit control ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 129.48pt, "and readout chips. This process enables a higher density of ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 141pt, "energy efficient ERSFQ circuits by lowering the minimum ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 153.24pt, "critical current to 10 ")
  #line-at(149.76pt, 153.24pt, "A and employing high resistivity ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 164.76pt, "junction shunts and a NbN high kinetic inductance layer ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 176.28pt, "(HKIL) for bias lines and circuit inductors with a target ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 187.68pt, "thickness of 40 nm and measured critical temperature of 11 K. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 199.2pt, "The fabricated chips were first tested in liquid helium at 4.2 K, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 210.72pt, "then in an adiabatic demagnetization refrigerator (ADR) from ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 222.24pt, "4.2 K down to 100 mK, and finally in a dilution refrigerator ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 233.76pt, "(DR) at about 10 mK. Importantly, the screening and testing ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 245.28pt, "of chips at 4.2 K in liquid helium proceeds much faster than at ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 256.68pt, "mK temperatures in ADR and/or DR due to much faster ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 268.2pt, "cooldown time and less complex and more developed test ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 279.72pt, "infrastructure. Therefore, one of the goals of this study is to be ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 291.24pt, "able to credibly predict the performance of ERSFQ circuits at ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 302.76pt, "10 mK solely by testing them at 4.2 K. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.8pt, 317.28pt, "A. Circuit Description ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(54pt, 331.68pt, "To study ERSFQ circuits at temperatures from 4.2 K to ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 343.2pt, "10 mK and to explain any changes in their performance, we ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 354.72pt, "designed a chip with both analog and digital PCMs. Since the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 366.24pt, "ERSFQ circuit performance is mainly influenced by ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 377.76pt, "Josephson ")
  #line-at(98.576pt, 377.76pt, "junction ")
  #line-at(141.993pt, 377.76pt, "(JJs) ")
  #line-at(170.905pt, 377.76pt, "critical ")
  #line-at(209.334pt, 377.76pt, "current ")
  #line-at(248.25pt, 377.76pt, "and ")
  #line-at(273.401pt, 377.76pt, "circuit ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 389.16pt, "inductances, we decided to study their dependence vs ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 400.68pt, "temperature in the range of interest. The analog PCMs include ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 412.92pt, "two arrays of ten nominally shunted 20-")
  #line-at(222pt, 412.92pt, "A and 100-")
  #line-at(275.88pt, 412.92pt, "A JJs ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 424.44pt, "each for monitoring the change of critical current (")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(274.8pt, 424.44pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(278.16pt, 425.4pt, "c")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(281.04pt, 424.44pt, ") vs ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 435.96pt, "temperature, and SQUID-based inductance test structures [24] ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 447.48pt, "to extract characteristic inductances of the NbN and Nb layers ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 459pt, "and their temperature dependences. The digital PCMs ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 470.52pt, "comprise five ERSFQ circuits, ordered by increasing ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 481.92pt, "complexity both in terms of JJ count and function: two chains ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 493.44pt, "of DC/SFQ-JTL-SFQ/DC with different DC/SFQ pickup ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 504.96pt, "coils; a frequency divider by 4 comprising two serially ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 516.48pt, "connected TFFs [25, 26]; a two port D-flip flop [27]; and an ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 528pt, "NDRO switch comprising an NDRO cell [28, 26] with ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 539.4pt, "synchronized set/reset inputs; respectively named sd1, sd2, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 550.92pt, "TFF, D2F and SW in following experimental graphs.  ")
  #line-at(54pt, 562.44pt, "We also tested circuits used in our experiments with digital ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 573.96pt, "qubit control at 4.2 K and 10 mK. These include a 1-to-4 ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 585.48pt, "demultiplexer (DMX) and an 8-bit programmable counter ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 597pt, "(PC), both NDRO based. The DMX features a single SFQ ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 608.4pt, "digital input that can be routed to four SFQ output channels. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 619.92pt, "Internally, the DMX is a serial-in, parallel-out shift register ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 631.44pt, "(SR) with non-destructive readout, with bits stored in the SR ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 642.96pt, "activating a path between the input and outputs [29]. Each ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 654.48pt, "serial pulse sent to the serial control interface shifts all bits in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 666pt, "the SR, while a clock pulse to the input will force the contents ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 677.4pt, "of the SR to the outputs, effectively passing the clock pulse to ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 688.92pt, "the selected outputs. The PC generates a user-determined ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 700.44pt, "number of clock pulses before stopping. Like the fixed ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 711.96pt, "counter, the PC [30, 10] has a chain of TFFs to track clock ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 723.48pt, "pulses. But whereas the fixed counter always counts to ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(286.92pt, 723.48pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(291.96pt, 720pt, "N")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(296.28pt, 723.48pt, ", ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 734.88pt, "where ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(73.8pt, 734.88pt, "N ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(82.92pt, 734.88pt, "is the number of TFFs, the programmable counter can ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 59.76pt, "count to any integer up to ")
