  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(560.16pt, 30.96pt, "4 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.8pt, 206.28pt, "Fig. 4.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(73.8pt, 206.28pt, " Temperature dependence of normalized center bias for ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 217.8pt, "five tested ERSFQ digital PCMs. See text for details. ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 235.32pt, "operation of the circuits in zero-voltage regime, when bias ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 246.72pt, "limiting JJs are not switching, and the least energy-efficient ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 258.24pt, "operation, when the bias limiting JJs are switching, providing ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 269.76pt, "the circuit with protection from the excessive bias current ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 281.28pt, "[36]. In the latter regime, when non-zero voltage is observed ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 292.8pt, "on the bias limiting junctions, the circuit still functions ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 304.2pt, "correctly, albeit by dissipating some additional power in the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 315.72pt, "bias-limiting JJs. On decreasing temperature, the bias margins ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 327.24pt, "for all ERSFQ PCMs in Fig. 5, from simplest DC/SFQ-JTL-")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 338.76pt, "SFQ/DC to most complex NDRO SW, monotonically ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 350.28pt, "decreased from as high as ±22% for the former PCM at 4.2 K ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 361.8pt, "to 5% for the latter one at 100 mK. Since PCMs were designed ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 373.2pt, "and optimized for 4.2 K operation, the change in margins can ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 384.72pt, "be also explained by the ~15% increase in ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(219.84pt, 384.72pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(223.2pt, 385.68pt, "c")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(226.08pt, 384.72pt, " of JJs from 4.2 K ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 396.24pt, "to 100 mK. ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 407.76pt, "Figs. 6 and 7 show experimental details for testing the 1-to-")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 419.28pt, "4 demultiplexer and 8-bit programmable counter to be used in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 430.8pt, "ERSFQ based digital qubit control [9, 17] (both NDRO ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 442.2pt, "based). Section IIA lists design details for the circuits and JJ ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 453.72pt, "counts. Fig. 6(b) and 7(b) display input and output signals of ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 465.24pt, "the functionality testing performed at ~2 MHz, with inputs ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 476.76pt, "supplied via current pulses sent to the chips’ DC-to-SFQ input ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 488.28pt, "converters, and digitized outputs representing SFQ pulses as ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 499.68pt, "jumps in voltage level. ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 511.2pt, "The DMX is programmed by a serial interface to a 4-cell ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 522.72pt, "memory register that corresponds to the 4 possible output ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 534.24pt, "channels. A ‘1’ bit in a memory cell allows SFQ pulses ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 545.76pt, "generated by a shared input to route through the associated  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(46.8pt, 709.56pt, "Fig. 5.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(76.92pt, 709.56pt, " Temperature dependence of operational total bias ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 720.96pt, "margins for five tested ERSFQ digital PCMs. See text for ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 732.48pt, "details. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.2pt, 172.32pt, "Fig. 6.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(346.2pt, 172.32pt, " Layout and results for 1-to-4 NDRO based ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 183.84pt, "demultiplexer: (a) circuit layout, (b) snapshot of input and ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 195.36pt, "output signals and (c) error rate vs bias current dependence.  ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 212.88pt, "output channel. The test pattern used here is a 4-channel ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 224.4pt, "rotation pattern. The register is first cleared with 4 serial clock ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 235.8pt, "pulses, then a single selection data bit is latched into the first ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 247.32pt, "memory cell. Four pulses are sent to the input to confirm they ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 258.84pt, "pass through to the first output channel (and no other outputs). ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 270.36pt, "Then a serial clock pulse moves the ‘1’ data bit to the next cell ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 281.88pt, "and the clock test is repeated for the second output. This ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 293.4pt, "process repeats until every cell of the DMX has been tested. ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 304.8pt, "The DMX test is considered a pass if no pulses are missing ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 316.32pt, "and there are also no extraneous pulses observed on a ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 327.84pt, "deselected channel. For the mK test, this full test pattern ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 339.36pt, "worked only intermittently with recurring problems observed ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 350.88pt, "on output 1. We believe this was caused by either trapped flux ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 362.4pt, "in the output 1 output monitor or a fabrication defect. The ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 373.8pt, "latter may also cause a nonzero error rate in the 4.2 K test and ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 385.32pt, "seems to be more plausible. Therefore, a simpler pattern was ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 396.84pt, "then tested where the register was cleared and only a single ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 408.36pt, "DMX channel was selected at a time with the serial interface, ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 419.88pt, "resulting in ±6% bias margins with zero error rate for outputs ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 431.4pt, "2 and 3. ")
  #line-at(323.28pt, 442.8pt, "For the PC, the number of pulses to be counted is ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 454.32pt, "programmed via a serial numeric data interface. Rising edges ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 465.84pt, "of the “serial data” signal latch a “1” bit into the first NDRO ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 477.36pt, "cell of the PC’s shift register. A subsequent rising edge of the ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 488.88pt, "serial clock moves these serial data bits from one cell to the ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 500.28pt, "next. There are 8 cells total in the serial memory register, ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 511.8pt, "enabling counts of any number between 1 and 256. Although ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 523.32pt, "multiple patterns were tested, the test pattern presented in Fig. ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 534.84pt, "7 programs the PC to count to 8, which fills the serial memory ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 546.36pt, "register with a mixture of 0 and 1 bits. This is a representative ")
  #line-at(313.2pt, 557.88pt, "pattern because it will produce clear error signatures if there ")
