  #line-at(46.8pt, 59.76pt, "the 8-bit counter, the PC only exhibited zero error rate with ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 71.28pt, "±5% bias margins at 4.2 K but never worked at 10 mK.  This ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 82.68pt, "can be explained by the increase in ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(189.36pt, 82.68pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(192.72pt, 83.64pt, "c")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(195.6pt, 82.68pt, " by ~15% bringing circuit ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 94.2pt, "bias outside of the operational margins. To bring the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(264.84pt, 94.2pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(268.2pt, 95.16pt, "c")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(274.2pt, 94.2pt, "down, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 105.72pt, "we employed an annealing process for ~30 minutes at 230℃ ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 117.24pt, "in ambient air.  This allows for relatively quick ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(239.76pt, 117.24pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(243.12pt, 118.2pt, "c")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(245.88pt, 117.24pt, " adjustments, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 128.76pt, "short of circuit redesign or fabrication process retargeting. By ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 140.28pt, "tuning annealing process parameters while simultaneously ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 151.68pt, "testing analog and digital PCMs, we were able  ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 163.2pt, "to reduce the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(101.04pt, 163.2pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(104.4pt, 164.16pt, "c")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(107.28pt, 163.2pt, " of the programmable counter by ~15%. After ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 174.72pt, "annealing, the counter operated with zero error with the same ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 186.24pt, "±5% margins as unannealed at 4.2 K.   ")
  #line-at(138.84pt, 209.76pt, "IV.")
  #line-at(153.96pt, 209.76pt, "C")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.025pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(160.56pt, 209.76pt, "ONCLUSION")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(56.88pt, 225.24pt, "We report on systematic testing in the temperature range ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 236.76pt, "from 4.2 K to 10 mK of a comprehensive set of analog PCMs, ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 248.28pt, "ERSFQ ")
  #line-at(88.415pt, 248.28pt, "cells, ")
  #line-at(119.937pt, 248.28pt, "and ")
  #line-at(145.187pt, 248.28pt, "more ")
  #line-at(176.381pt, 248.28pt, "complex ")
  #line-at(221.452pt, 248.28pt, "circuits ")
  #line-at(261.463pt, 248.28pt, "such ")
  #line-at(290.422pt, 248.28pt, "as ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 259.68pt, "demultiplexers and programmable counters used in digital ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 271.2pt, "qubit control. We compare the operating margins and error ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 282.72pt, "rates of these circuits and find that the center of bias margins ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 294.24pt, "(i.e., the optimal bias current value) for the tested circuits ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 305.76pt, "increases by ~15% from 4.2 K to millikelvin. In the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 317.16pt, "temperature range of interest, the measured Josephson ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 328.68pt, "junction (JJ) critical current ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(162.96pt, 328.68pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(166.32pt, 329.64pt, "c")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(172.32pt, 328.68pt, "of the PCM JJ arrays increases ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 340.2pt, "by ~15%, in good agreement with both theory and measured ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 351.72pt, "change of the center of bias margins for the tested digital ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 363.24pt, "circuits. In contrast, the geometrical and kinetic inductances ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 374.76pt, "(Nb and NbN layers, respectively) were not affected by the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 386.16pt, "change in temperature. The operational bias margins for ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 397.68pt, "ERSFQ PCM and qubit control circuits designed to operate at ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 409.2pt, "4.2 K decreased as temperature dropped, with this decrease in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 420.72pt, "functional range getting more pronounced with an increase in ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 432.24pt, "circuit complexity. The operational margins at millikelvin ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 443.76pt, "completely disappeared for the most complex circuit, the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 455.16pt, "programmable counter, and the circuit was not functional at ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 466.68pt, "any point in the measured bias range. With ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(225.96pt, 466.68pt, "I")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.468pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(229.32pt, 467.64pt, "c")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.941pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(232.2pt, 466.68pt, " of the junctions ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 478.2pt, "of the counter reduced by ~15% by means of annealing, the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 489.72pt, "counter maintained operational bias margins at millikelvin ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 501.24pt, "comparable to the margins of the unannealed counter at 4.2 K.  ")
  #line-at(56.88pt, 512.76pt, "Our results confirm that with simple adjustment, the ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 524.16pt, "ERSFQ circuits used for qubit control are able to operate at ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 535.68pt, "millikelvin temperatures with similar bias margins as at their ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 547.2pt, "design temperature of 4.2 K. This can be achieved by design ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 558.72pt, "modification to account for critical current change, retargeting ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 570.24pt, "of fabrication process critical current density, or post-")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 581.64pt, "processing annealing. Our results pave the way for high-speed ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 593.16pt, "and low-power superconducting electronics to be proximally ")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 604.68pt, "integrated with qubits for digital control, readout, and co-")
  #line-at(46.8pt, 616.2pt, "processing for low-latency real-time QEC. ")
